  "id": "primary-attention",
  "term": "primary attention",
  "definition": "Primary attention is a historical term for the supposed form of attention, or an organic counterpart of it, in very simple organisms that are thought too undeveloped to have a life of mental presentations. The source indicates that if attention is used in this sense, it should be qualified as 'primary.'",
